  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nIntermittent light rain from late today through Wednesday \nmorning. A bit of drought relief in Northern Maine.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nIncreasing clouds from the west today but mild with highs in the\nlow to mid 60s. A chance of light rain starting late afternoon,\nwith some areas of light rain continuing to develop into\ntonight. Late tonight and into Tuesday, a backdoor cold front\nslides through from NE to SW, cooling off temperatures. Then\nanother upper level disturbance moves in from the west and we\nwill see overrunning steady rainfall late Tuesday through\nWednesday morning. The backdoor cold front will reverse\ndirection and move back NE as a warm front, and after the warm\nfront moves through the entire area by midday Wednesday,\nrainfall ends. We have more confidence in a decent soaking rain\nin the north, with likely at least one half inch from Presque\nIsle north, with amounts maybe even approaching one inch in the\nSt John Valley. Amounts look lighter the further south you go,\nwith around or a bit less than one quarter inch.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for significant rain at some point in\nthe late Thursday through late Saturday timeframe, but \nconfidence is still fairly low in timing and amounts.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA lull in the action from Wednesday afternoon through Thursday,\nwith a fairly warm airmass over the region. Thursday should\nfeature 60s, with perhaps a few places reaching 70. Then rain\nchances increase for the late Thursday to late Saturday period.\nThere is still a lot of uncertainty in the evolution of an\napproaching upper level trough and potential developing surface\nlow pressure, but the ingredients exist for a strong storm\nsystem and soaking rain at some point in this time period. Right\nnow, it looks like about a 50-60 percent chance of at least an\ninch of rain late Thursday to late Saturday, with no part of the\nstate being more obviously favored over another. There is even a\n10-15 percent chance of over 3 inches of rain. Depending on the\ntrack of a potential low pressure system, winds could be an \nissue as well, but there is very low confidence on this.",
